        "claim_id": "executive_summary",
        "tier": "descriptive",
        "modality": "report",
        "analysis": "executive_summary",
        "text": "To address age-related chromatin accessibility changes in the human hippocampus, scATAC-seq analysis of 3,000 cells identified 10,022 differentially accessible peaks across 11 clusters with medium confidence. Motif enrichment analysis of these peaks, tested against 879 JASPAR2024 motifs, revealed significant enrichment in 9 of the 11 cluster groups. However, the absence of FRiP and TSS enrichment metrics limits the assessment of data quality and regulatory specificity. Validation of specific peak-to-gene links and functional characterization of the enriched transcription factors are required to establish causal regulatory mechanisms.",
